SPECIFICATION: DX7-style 6-operator FM synthesizer (Python / Pygame)

GOAL
Recreate a standalone desktop FM synth that sounds like a Yamaha DX7, with
pre-rendered loopable samples, per-note ADSR playback, a large guitar-pedal
effects rack baked at generate-time, computer-keyboard + MIDI input, and a
Pygame GUI. Single file preferred: dx7.py.

DEPENDENCIES
- Python 3.9+
- pygame 2.x (mixer, display, optional pygame.midi)
- numpy
No other packages. No network.

RUNTIME / FILES (same directory as dx7.py)
- site.key            optional keymap; tokens like z48 (key then MIDI number)
- fm_window.json      {w,h,x,y} window geometry
- fm_bank.json        list of patches
- tones/              created if missing
    <SafeName>.json       full patch + effects + chain
    <SafeName>.dat.npz    cached waveforms (also accept .npz / .dat)

CONSTANTS
SAMPLE_RATE=44100, NOTE_SECONDS=5.0, XFADE_SEC=0.06, MAX_POLY=16
DEFAULT_ADSR = {a:0.02, d:0.12, s:0.85, r:0.25}  seconds, s is 0..1
DEFAULT_KEYMAP if site.key missing:
  "z48 s49 x50 d51 c52 v53 g54 b55 h56 n57 j58 m59 ,60 l61 .62 /64
   q60 261 w62 363 e64 r65 566 t67 668 y69 770 u71 i72 o73 p74 [76 ]77"

==============================================================================
FM ENGINE (first-iteration per-sample renderer)
==============================================================================
6 operators. Each op:
  on:bool, level:0-99, coarse:0-31 (0 means ratio 0.5), fine:0-99 (cents-ish /1000),
  detune:-7..+7, rates:[r1..r4] 0-99, levels:[l1..l4] 0-99

Algorithms (carriers / modulators / feedback op index). Use at least:
  1, 2, 5, 16, 18, 32
Example algo 2: carriers [0,2]; mods 0<-1, 2<-3<-4<-5; feedback on op 1.

Per sample:
  for ops 5..0:
    mod = sum(values of modulator ops)
    if this op is feedback op: mod += last[op] * ((feedback/7)^2 * 4)
    value = sin(phase + mod) * env * (1.2 if modulator else 1.0)
    phase += 2π * f0 * ratio * 2^(detune*0.03/12) / SAMPLE_RATE
  mix carriers, normalize, * 0.22 * velocity scale, clip [-1,1]

Operator EG: 4-rate / 4-level DX-ish exponential approach.
sec = 0.003 + (1 - rate/99)^2 * 3.5
coeff = 1 - exp(-1/(sec*sr))
Advance stages 0->1->2 while held.

Looping:
  Drop ~0.35s attack from buffer, equal-power crossfade XFADE_SEC at wrap
  (cos out * tail + sin in * head), remove DC, peak-normalize to 0.97.

ONLY generate samples for MIDI notes present in the keymap.
Rebuild samples ONLY when:
  - patch operators/algo/feedback/name change and user APPLY / dropdown close
    with fingerprint change
  - GENERATE in effects dialog (force + bake FX)
  - create patch
NEVER rebuild on every key press. ADSR changes do NOT rebuild samples.

==============================================================================
PLAYBACK
==============================================================================
pygame.mixer: pre_init then init BEFORE set_mode (macOS crash otherwise).
set_num_channels(MAX_POLY). Mono int16 Sound objects, loops=-1 while held.

PlayingNote per voice:
  Independent ADSR on CHANNEL VOLUME only.
  Attack 0->1 over a, decay 1->s over d, sustain s, on release fade from
  current level to 0 over r. ADSR does not reset at loop points.
  Voices independent. Voice stealing: drop oldest when poly full.
  On same-note retrigger, stop previous voice first.
  Scope: mix current playhead windows of all active waves * their ADSR levels.

==============================================================================
PATCHES
==============================================================================
Factory bank, Jump FIRST:
  Jump (algo 2, fb 7) brass-like two-carrier stack, then E.Piano, Tight Piano,
  Tubular Bell, Marimba, Music Box, Vibraphone, Jazz Organ, Church Organ,
  FM Bass, Slap Bass, Jazz Flute, Pan Flute, Syn Brass, Trumpet, Alto Sax,
  Warm Strings, Choir Aahs, Soft Pad, Clavinet, Nylon Guitar, Steel Guitar,
  Tuba, INIT.

ensure_adsr() on load. Missing ADSR → defaults.
EDIT without renaming still saves full patch including ADSR into bank.
Tone JSON stores {patch, effects, chain}. Load JSON when selecting a patch.
If .dat.npz exists, load waves; else render and save.

Fingerprint for rebuild: JSON of patch minus adsr.

==============================================================================
INPUT
==============================================================================
Parse site.key tokens: letters/symbols then integer MIDI.
Keys 1-6 and specifically 2,3,4,6 are NOTE KEYS ONLY. Never bind them to
operator select or envelope edits. Operator select = OP1..OP6 buttons only.
Optional Ctrl+O/Q/A/W/S/E/D for op on/level/coarse/detune — never digits.

MIDI: cycle inputs with MIDI CONNECT. Note on/off 0x90/0x80.

Effects dialog OPEN must still play mapped keys.
Exception: while search box focused, keys type into search.
Up/Down/PgUp/PgDn/Home/End navigate the effects list.

==============================================================================
GUI (Pygame, resizable)
==============================================================================
Restore window size/position from fm_window.json; save on resize/quit.
SDL_VIDEO_WINDOW_POS before set_mode.

Layout:
- Top buttons: CREATE, LOAD, EDIT, MIDI CONNECT, APPLY, SAVE ADSR, EFFECTS
- Patch dropdown under CREATE. Generate samples only when list CLOSES and
  patch fingerprint changed.
- ALG-/ALG+ FB-/FB+
- OP1..OP6
- Panel: selected op readout, status
- THREE ALIGNED graphs same Y and height (~y=200,h=150):
  OP envelope | Playback ADSR | Oscilloscope (sum of all voices)
- ADSR sliders A,D,S,R under graphs. SAVE ADSR writes bank, no sample regen.
- Centered on-screen keyboard spanning ALL mapped MIDI notes, labels from keymap.

Patch dialog: name field, Enter saves, Escape cancels.
CREATE inserts at index 0 and force-renders.

==============================================================================
EFFECTS
==============================================================================
Button EFFECTS opens modal. Layout:
  Left: search box + scrollable checkbox list of ALL effects (80+).
  Right top: CHAIN bar. Click opens FULL-HEIGHT overlay listing every stage
  in selection order; overlay draws ON TOP of the pedal, wheel-scrollable.
  Check = append to chain. Uncheck = remove from chain. Order = selection order.
  GENERATE writes tone JSON and re-renders every mapped note, applying
  apply_fx_chain(wave, fx_state, chain) then make_loopable.

Sliders NEVER overlay the pedal graphic. They sit BELOW it.
Knobs on the pedal: one knob per slider, same page as sliders.
Page of 6 knobs/sliders; mouse wheel over pedal OR slider pane advances page.
Every knob labeled with shortened name (alnum, max ~6 chars).

Pedal text contrast:
  Light paint (luma>=150): black / dark blue / purple text.
  Dark paint: white / yellow / pink text.

Knob / needle:
  Dark pedal → light (cream) knob, needle BLACK or DARK BLUE.
  Light pedal → dark knob, needle WHITE.
  Needle must contrast the knob face.

TW / NUX / PH9 (exact controls):
  Mosky Audio TW Distortion: knobs gain,bass,mid,treble,presence,level
    switch modern (off=VINTAGE soft clip, on=MODERN hard clip + tighter HPF)
  NUX Roctary: knobs speed,balance,horn,drive,oct_mix,dry,tone,level
    switches fast, poly, rotary
  Behringer PH9: knob rate; switch color (4 vs 6 stages)
Put these three near the TOP of the list so they are easy to find.

Effects catalog must include at least:
  Gain/saturation, clean/treble/mid boost, preamp, Klon, BluesBreaker,
  Tube Screamer, RAT, DS-1, high-gain metal, Big Muff, Fuzz Face, octave fuzz,
  Super Fuzz, Ultra Vibrato, Ibanez FL9, Funky Monkey, Swollen Pickle,
  Plexibox, Ravish Sitar, TW Dist, PH9, comp/sustainer, bitcrusher,
  compressor/limiter, expander, gate, volume/swell, tremolo (optical/bias/harmonic),
  transient shaper, graphic EQ, 6/10/20-param EQ, exciter, wah, auto-wah,
  Q-filter, talk box, formant, chorus, flanger, phaser (EVH red stripes),
  vibrato, uni-vibe, rotary/Leslie, ring mod, freq shifter, auto-pan,
  harmonic tremolo, octave/POG, pitch shift, harmonizer (pink), whammy, detune,
  delay (tape/analog/reverse/pingpong/mod/shimmer switches),
  reverb (spring/plate/hall/room/cathedral/shimmer/freeze/gated/reverse),
  looper, freeze, granular/glitch, acoustic sim, amp sim, cab/IR, mic/room,
  multi-fx, tuner, buffer, A/B, expression, PSU, wireless,
  wah-fuzz, fuzz+filter, delay+reverb, trem+reverb, OD+boost, comp+OD,
  synth+octave, granular delay, spectral freeze, vocoder, overdrive, tube,
  8-bit, tape echo, slapback, lo-fi, comb, soft sat, NUX Roctary.

DSP is bake-time numpy (one-pole LPF, HPF=x-lpf, tanh soft clip, hard clip,
comb delay, pitch resample, LFO). Chain applied in fx_chain order.
Peak-normalize after chain.

Pedal colors (examples): RAT black, overdrive green, reverb purple, chorus blue,
harmonizer pink, phaser/PH9 red + EVH stripes, TW near-black.

==============================================================================
INIT ORDER (macOS)
==============================================================================
mixer.pre_init(44100,-16,1,512)
set SDL_VIDEO_WINDOW_POS
pygame.init()
if mixer not init: mixer.init(...)
mixer.set_num_channels(MAX_POLY)
display.set_mode(RESIZABLE)

==============================================================================
NON-GOALS / RULES
==============================================================================
- Do not use keys 2,3,4,6 (or 1-6) as edit shortcuts.
- Do not regenerate samples on ADSR or on every keydown.
- Do not overlay sliders on the pedal art.
- Do not hide a long FX chain behind the pedal; use a topmost scroll panel.
- Oscilloscope shows the SUM of playing notes, not a single oscillator.